#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161800 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6289ad34-2393-5f5f-b7f0-a1ab1a3916f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Quadratic Form Types Using Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "f3f6f5b1-bc25-586c-9d4d-dfeb64cfa077" :question/math-academy-id "e-8262" :question/problem "Consider the vector ![](images/cc/cc0456884aa670c8c7f86387574a187f151f4ccc4e4275671425af1aa61812e8.png) By evaluating the following quadratic forms at $\\mathbf{x}$ **only,** determine which of them **cannot** be negative-definite.\n\n- $R(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2 - 3x_2^2 + 5x_1x_2$\n\n- ![](images/ac/acf8b72ee7b927e5e82570c655a671a62b595a29c8191a64ad22ac98af8cf7a4.png)\n\n- $T(\\mathbf{x})=x_2^2 + 8x_1x_2$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is negative-definite if $Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\lt 0$ for all $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\setminus \\{ \\mathbf{0} \\}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the quadratic forms by substituting ![](images/29/29545f79f3b34ca5395f98fa8c8c81e289482e866c3ad8c576aeb7b9fe8b8749.png)\n\n- Quadratic form I *might* be negative-definite. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(x) & ={2}^{2}-3\\cdot {7}^{2}+5\\cdot 2\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =4-147+70 \\\\  & =-73<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form II *cannot* be negative-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 14\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =110>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form III *cannot* be negative-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(x) & ={7}^{2}+8\\cdot 2\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =49+112 \\\\  & =161>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161801 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4105f1cb-eb48-5946-92f7-cd5e67689912" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type by Calculating the Corresponding Eigenvalues"}] :question/id #uuid "178e4bbc-718c-5b9e-843a-91914ef16f64" :question/math-academy-id "e-8263" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/d1/d16c12fa9086e956b3b0516d42b40aaa121e3b40bd25a72c3d05d436ba410440.png) Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\lambda_1=-1$ and $\\lambda_2=9$\n\n- $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\, \\mathbf{x}$ is indefinite\n\n- $A$ is positive-definite" :question/worked-solution "Given a quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf x) = \\mathbf{x}^T A \\mathbf{x},$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the characteristic equation of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-25 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda -9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =1,\\,-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Since $A$ has positive and negative eigenvalues, the quadratic form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\, \\mathbf{x}$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is indefinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161802 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/id #uuid "fa658f82-1d0b-54a3-a172-4d59f03f629e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8264" :question/problem "![](images/d8/d81ce57017adec7daf2556322259f32ce4261e646dc8f1a48632beb085d9a9cb.png)\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $a_{11}=-6$ and $\\det(A) \\lt 0$\n\n- $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\, \\mathbf{x}$ is negative-definite\n\n- $A$ is positive-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\Delta_i$ for $i=1,2,\\ldots,n$  denote the principal minors of an $n \\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\, \\mathbf{x}$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if $\\Delta_i > 0$ for all $i=1,2,\\ldots,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,\\ldots,n,$ we have $\\Delta_i <          0$ when $i$ is odd, and $\\Delta_i > 0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $a_{11}=-6.$ Expanding $\\det(A)$ along the top row, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-6)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-5)|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-6)(-2)+(5)(-7)+12 \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-6<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|=37>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-11<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\, \\mathbf{x},$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daa79a2c-7393-51fd-aa68-53f7bcbfd36a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449532} {:answer/id #uuid "3d7d5d0c-57fa-5f8d-a238-f9a8292d8c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d7d5d0c-57fa-5f8d-a238-f9a8292d8c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449533} :answer-field/id #uuid "aebff15a-46bb-5e25-b5f7-52cc4f246811" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450720} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1909387-b83c-52db-b6e3-ab497516fded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449534} {:answer/id #uuid "8eebe797-5a30-55f7-8a3a-e1cba2f6d82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1909387-b83c-52db-b6e3-ab497516fded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449534} :answer-field/id #uuid "79794586-10dc-5ee4-b484-f880ca056d6d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f5b011-a5ec-5e29-8cff-d8e9fe83ea41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449536} {:answer/id #uuid "158c0776-5611-5095-a30f-0b3db7bfac21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08f5b011-a5ec-5e29-8cff-d8e9fe83ea41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449536} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2987329-85fb-5d6c-a910-7bce43831da5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "906865b3-32d2-5d7f-b7fc-d38ff3d60bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-139462" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=2$ and $det(A)=-3$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is negative-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=2$ and \n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-3.\n$$\n\n- Statements II and  III are false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=2>0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-3<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, neither the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ nor the matrix $A$ is positive-definite or negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4105f1cb-eb48-5946-92f7-cd5e67689912" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type by Calculating the Corresponding Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8385fb50-741c-52a9-b66d-7f14ebf47fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448786} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d11be8-de44-538d-b685-8fbb9971c1c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8385fb50-741c-52a9-b66d-7f14ebf47fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448786} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3395e9e-2ed4-5a34-b396-23c884a38c4d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449433} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bafa656d-caf1-53a6-b60d-6d69b564a720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448788} {:answer/id #uuid "1cbd03fa-0bf1-53b5-887b-a59ab5e51a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bafa656d-caf1-53a6-b60d-6d69b564a720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448788} :answer-field/id #uuid "870750d0-d594-59b5-bae0-7b99729a4ee6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449434} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffbc9d5a-becc-5a3e-a1e6-639ca76f2d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448790} {:answer/id #uuid "42d3491e-c999-568a-be45-5ecce2260933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42d3491e-c999-568a-be45-5ecce2260933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448791} :answer-field/id #uuid "64499da8-7609-5129-bde6-6636fa8e16a1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb99fd8a-40c2-5ae9-b122-b1e03bf9e31a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94465" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=7$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=10$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is indefinite" :question/worked-solution "Given a quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}Ax,$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the characteristic equation of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}9-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -70 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-7,\\,10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Since $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is indefinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8704f06e-0eca-5a70-9700-c5526052b2a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460407} {:answer/id #uuid "6518d566-4b59-5853-9f01-fa65f41a11a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8704f06e-0eca-5a70-9700-c5526052b2a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460407} :answer-field/id #uuid "328cbc85-02de-5782-9f6f-1bfc8ec8fbb3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b050a0c6-7aec-5f7e-8f14-b631435a1e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460409} {:answer/id #uuid "7dea8288-7e98-5761-9e3b-5108736ab6b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dea8288-7e98-5761-9e3b-5108736ab6b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460410} :answer-field/id #uuid "147acc30-38f6-5dd4-b1fc-756ff6c1cd6a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70cc8a99-fd5f-545d-944d-b10871efed96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460411} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4651ad-1ec2-5084-a1f5-126f6778fe6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70cc8a99-fd5f-545d-944d-b10871efed96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460411} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6975a47-d056-596c-bc2f-5293e337fd67" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a18cc33-e8b9-51a0-9ec6-b247bdd1e062" :question/math-academy-id "q-94467" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=-1$ and $det(A)>0$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is positive-definite\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-1$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-4<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-1<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}|=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-4<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6289ad34-2393-5f5f-b7f0-a1ab1a3916f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Quadratic Form Types Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491282d8-087a-5b6a-872d-6b0a47d66b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469722} {:answer/id #uuid "06e9071d-b647-5c18-bb45-e68fcc570e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491282d8-087a-5b6a-872d-6b0a47d66b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469722} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef7d7514-e7a3-5427-b315-a9a69bce3495" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83d2a2f4-ca6f-5c88-a824-d7acfdea58ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469724} {:answer/id #uuid "95ece7a6-9e69-5e78-8957-46a3c4175115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95ece7a6-9e69-5e78-8957-46a3c4175115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469725} :answer-field/id #uuid "64c56b6b-2880-560b-9538-f33060b8721c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470474} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5da7956-0eb9-5adb-bdb6-5c327d8b35b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469726} {:answer/id #uuid "91c1f39d-20a8-532f-b2ef-a41f48e42975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91c1f39d-20a8-532f-b2ef-a41f48e42975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469727} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4dd36d1-3aac-54c6-b8e2-1006ae8abc43" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96ce050e-6292-5b2a-b7c7-0c1f7f51192d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94731" :question/problem "$$\n\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ By evaluating the following quadratic forms at $x$ **only,** determine which of them **cannot** be negative-definite.\n- **I.** $R(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$\n- **II.** $S(x)={x}^{T}\\,[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]x$\n- **III.** $T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form $Q(x)$ is negative-definite if $Q(x)<0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the quadratic forms by substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n- Quadratic form I *might* be negative-definite. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(x) & =(-1)^{2}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =1-9 \\\\  & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form II *cannot* be negative-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =33>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form III *cannot* be negative-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(x) & =(-1)^{2}+3(3)^{2} \\\\  & =1+27 \\\\  & =28>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6289ad34-2393-5f5f-b7f0-a1ab1a3916f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Quadratic Form Types Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed9f53d-8f5a-5d51-9fe5-b5701dfd17d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452059} {:answer/id #uuid "ba149761-6f03-59d5-b0a6-561327764bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ed9f53d-8f5a-5d51-9fe5-b5701dfd17d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452059} :answer-field/id #uuid "943f3044-0061-5817-a4df-8dc03a7939e6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452877} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d04386a-bf21-5e45-9825-7bc717ea9952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452061} {:answer/id #uuid "b350b539-18ee-52b0-bf06-3473cf1e8fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b350b539-18ee-52b0-bf06-3473cf1e8fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452062} :answer-field/id #uuid "1504f3a0-fa56-5d2a-8097-b25f32f379f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6da48a5-41d7-502e-b0c3-5047cccb111f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452063} {:answer/id #uuid "a640cd11-4a14-590a-9fa1-6e2e6e1f2e6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6da48a5-41d7-502e-b0c3-5047cccb111f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452063} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fc57d82-6dd3-56dd-bc98-4625624ce330" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08e6755d-cc77-5492-aef8-539543b12cc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94744" :question/problem "Which of the following statements regarding quadratic forms are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R(x)=8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ is positive-definite\n- **II.** $S(x)={x}^{T}\\,[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]x$ is negative-definite\n- **III.** $T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}$ is indefinite" :question/worked-solution "Recall that, a quadratic form $Q(x)$ is:\n\n- positive-definite if $Q(x)>0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0};$\n\n- negative-definite if $Q(x)<0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0};$\n\n- indefinite if \n\n- $Q({x}_{1})>0$ for some ${x}_{1}\\in {R}^{n},$ and\n\n- $Q({x}_{2})<0$ for some ${x}_{2}\\in {R}^{n}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Substituting ${x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R({x}_{1}) & =8\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting ${x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R({x}_{2}) & =8\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the quadratic form is indefinite.\n\n- Statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-(2{x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2})<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0}.$ So, the quadratic form is negative-definite.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0},$ the quadratic form is positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4105f1cb-eb48-5946-92f7-cd5e67689912" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type by Calculating the Corresponding Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f98de070-157f-534d-80ca-0285e5ea31dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452083} {:answer/id #uuid "174de886-386b-5d7b-a04e-97378dcc50c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "174de886-386b-5d7b-a04e-97378dcc50c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452084} :answer-field/id #uuid "e799f149-b778-5e67-89e1-41f4feb99d40" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4d1217-ff6e-508b-b3bc-dea5acc63146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452085} {:answer/id #uuid "78c882b5-c654-506d-9f34-f6de960b4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78c882b5-c654-506d-9f34-f6de960b4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452086} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb439c2a-82f5-579a-b442-b6cef060ee5e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dbe70c7-c5db-5456-9d9f-eceb402243d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452087} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3f8a7a-53c9-58ba-8c93-06d4c7b15b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dbe70c7-c5db-5456-9d9f-eceb402243d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452087} :answer-field/id #uuid "b68b3e83-f797-507a-a054-d24715a897e1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13d1d5cf-031d-5ebf-8e4c-d550f344afdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-94795" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is indefinite" :question/worked-solution "Given a quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}Ax,$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the characteristic equation of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =1,\\,5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Since all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e6b6069-a73e-55b4-8237-8d4f4f222dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452089} {:answer/id #uuid "db8fa190-5652-57d4-9d6f-36a68e1d279f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db8fa190-5652-57d4-9d6f-36a68e1d279f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452090} :answer-field/id #uuid "88f61762-6f70-5d21-b1c1-800aae0f2fff" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311261b6-23c6-5a90-af11-2891a6bef398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452091} {:answer/id #uuid "3e682b91-127f-5abb-bc3a-e837723de4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e682b91-127f-5abb-bc3a-e837723de4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452092} :answer-field/id #uuid "4558c17e-723a-50fc-8a86-1acb9b4e8d09" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bedbf47f-c0ac-5fc5-a3f5-ee511e9a5b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452093} {:answer/id #uuid "1a766f1d-8b11-5027-b338-059d385649a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a766f1d-8b11-5027-b338-059d385649a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452094} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdfd5bb3-65c5-50b4-abd6-2525ca2c0e80" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81d008a7-fd35-5fff-9f9d-fc0e8e60bfec" :question/math-academy-id "q-94797" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=2$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is negative-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-3$ and \n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=2.\n$$\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-3<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=2>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea1b93a-38ba-5c72-9bee-3fbe580f05cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452113} {:answer/id #uuid "81ba5de2-4ec0-55fe-bab8-33d6d9253f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ba5de2-4ec0-55fe-bab8-33d6d9253f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452114} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f57c56b-b2e1-58e7-8141-026fa0dded98" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85c12093-8dda-5103-9819-5b62a8cc94b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452115} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e0ca83-7bc5-54f5-b90f-2bcba9b76ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c12093-8dda-5103-9819-5b62a8cc94b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452115} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dc9ccf9-fe82-5943-aefd-c2e968dec187" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2dacb8-3a73-5142-9d28-821696fba02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452117} {:answer/id #uuid "07437bee-0a6c-5947-bc81-ab31e28f0bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07437bee-0a6c-5947-bc81-ab31e28f0bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4392f3-f738-5e5a-88d9-29ab52adafd4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0bcde67-e6f1-5859-87e0-ff664264d2ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-94806" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=-6$ and $det(A)<0$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is negative-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-6$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-6<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}|=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-6<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
